  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21880356",
      "title": "Using Vuex with the Composition API",
      "lectureOrder": 307,
      "videoOrder": 274,
      "sourceHash": "6deb046e3ab3111303a2eb695de11e4aa52a5cfdd190f9b29ab04ba47a938de9",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.12,
          "end": 4.37,
          "en": "Now we know how we can use routing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.37,
          "end": 6.04,
          "en": "with the composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.04,
          "end": 7.58,
          "en": "What about Vuex?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.58,
          "end": 10.9,
          "en": "How can we use that with the composition API?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.9,
          "end": 12.73,
          "en": "For this, attached you find another",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.73,
          "end": 15.05,
          "en": "very simple dummy project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.05,
          "end": 16.5,
          "en": "We've got a counter there and a button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 16.5,
          "end": 18.43,
          "en": "which currently does nothing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 18.43,
          "end": 20.87,
          "en": "but this is built with the composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 20.87,
          "end": 22.95,
          "en": "I mean, these are very simple components,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 22.95,
          "end": 26.21,
          "en": "but I plan on using the composition API there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 26.21,
          "end": 29.87,
          "en": "The App.vue file is pretty straightforward and simple,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.87,
          "end": 32.05,
          "en": "just a couple of local components here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 32.05,
          "end": 34.62,
          "en": "And then in the counter, I output the counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 34.62,
          "end": 38.39,
          "en": "but I plan on getting the counter with the composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.39,
          "end": 40.9,
          "en": "At the moment I just have a dummy counter here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 40.9,
          "end": 42.61,
          "en": "which does never change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 42.61,
          "end": 44.43,
          "en": "And in the control center,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 44.43,
          "end": 47.3,
          "en": "I also plan on defining this function with the composition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 47.3,
          "end": 51.25,
          "en": "API, but at the moment, it's does nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 51.25,
          "end": 53.367,
          "en": "Now, obviously we don't need Vuex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 53.367,
          "end": 55.44,
          "en": "for this simple of an application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 55.44,
          "end": 57.56,
          "en": "We don't need Vuex for this demo,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 57.56,
          "end": 61.366,
          "en": "but I want to show you how you can utilize Vuex with the",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 61.366,
          "end": 64.52,
          "en": "composition API in case you're building more complex",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 64.52,
          "end": 66.93,
          "en": "projects where you need Vuex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 66.93,
          "end": 68.75,
          "en": "So how does this work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 68.75,
          "end": 72.32,
          "en": "In main JS, I already set up a store with createStore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 72.32,
          "end": 74.65,
          "en": "as you learned in the Vuex module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 74.65,
          "end": 78.87,
          "en": "I have a state, mutations, an action and a getter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 78.87,
          "end": 80.97,
          "en": "And how can we now utilize that store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 80.97,
          "end": 84.98,
          "en": "which I'm already using in my app, in these components?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.98,
          "end": 86.9,
          "en": "Well, just as the router,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 86.9,
          "end": 91.61,
          "en": "the Vue router offered us a custom composition function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 91.61,
          "end": 94.81,
          "en": "which we could call inside of our setup method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 94.81,
          "end": 96.63,
          "en": "to use routing features.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 96.63,
          "end": 99.92,
          "en": "Just as the router did this, the Vuex package has",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.92,
          "end": 101.89,
          "en": "something similar in store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.89,
          "end": 103.64,
          "en": "So in the control center,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 103.64,
          "end": 107.45,
          "en": "where I in the end want to dispatch the increment action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 107.45,
          "end": 112.44,
          "en": "I can import something from Vuex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 113.66,
          "end": 117.87,
          "en": "And that something, is the useStore hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 117.87,
          "end": 120.14,
          "en": "or the useStore composable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 120.14,
          "end": 123.41,
          "en": "The useStore custom composition function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 123.41,
          "end": 127.93,
          "en": "which is meant to be executed inside of the setup method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 127.93,
          "end": 130.91,
          "en": "Here we can then call useStore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 130.91,
          "end": 133.46,
          "en": "and what we get as a result is access to the...",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 133.46,
          "end": 135.23,
          "en": "well to the Vuex store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 135.23,
          "end": 137.78,
          "en": "which we have attached to this application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 137.78,
          "end": 142.78,
          "en": "So the Vuex store, we are using with Use here on our app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 143.53,
          "end": 146.55,
          "en": "We get access to that store by calling useStore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 146.55,
          "end": 147.623,
          "en": "inside of setup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 148.53,
          "end": 151.99,
          "en": "Well, and once we got access it'll of course be simple.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 151.99,
          "end": 154.48,
          "en": "We can just use store, dispatch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 154.48,
          "end": 157.23,
          "en": "and then dispatch the action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 157.23,
          "end": 159.82999999999998,
          "en": "So dispatch any action, like in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 159.82999999999998,
          "end": 164.07,
          "en": "the increment action, which we registered on this store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 164.07,
          "end": 167.22,
          "en": "And you can then use any Vuex feature you learn about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.22,
          "end": 170.32999999999998,
          "en": "Modules, namespacing... all of that is available.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 170.32999999999998,
          "end": 174.31,
          "en": "And you just use useStore to get access to the store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.31,
          "end": 177.01,
          "en": "instead of using this dollar sign store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 177.01,
          "end": 179.3,
          "en": "which you would use if you would be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 179.3,
          "end": 181.223,
          "en": "working with the options API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 182.3,
          "end": 184.87,
          "en": "Well, and therefore it's the same here in the counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 184.87,
          "end": 188.74,
          "en": "where I want to get access to some data stored in the store.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 188.74,
          "end": 193.74,
          "en": "I can simply import useStore from Vuex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 195.03,
          "end": 199.353,
          "en": "Then, get access to the store by calling useStore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.35,
          "end": 203.61,
          "en": "And thereafter when we want to get a counter that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 203.61,
          "end": 206.07999999999998,
          "en": "depends on a getter in the store,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 206.07999999999998,
          "end": 208.62,
          "en": "we just need to create a computed variable,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 208.62,
          "end": 213.27,
          "en": "a computed value just as we do it in the options API world.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.27,
          "end": 218.04,
          "en": "So therefore we import computed from Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.04,
          "end": 221.59,
          "en": "and then counter should be a computed value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.59,
          "end": 223.25,
          "en": "by calling computed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 223.25,
          "end": 226.68,
          "en": "where we provide a function that will be executed whenever",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 226.68,
          "end": 228.69,
          "en": "one of its dependencies changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 228.69,
          "end": 230.24,
          "en": "And here in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 230.24,
          "end": 234.74,
          "en": "we returned store.getters.counter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 234.74,
          "end": 238.883,
          "en": "because counter is the getter name I defined here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 240.7,
          "end": 243.64,
          "en": "And whenever the counter changes, Vue will detect this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 243.64,
          "end": 246.677,
          "en": "in the end and recalculate this computed value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 246.677,
          "end": 249.21,
          "en": "which we then expose to the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 249.21,
          "end": 252.52,
          "en": "And since you learned that computed values are refs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 252.52,
          "end": 254.3,
          "en": "whatever the counter does change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.3,
          "end": 257.42,
          "en": "Vue will notice this and it will update the template",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 257.42,
          "end": 259.713,
          "en": "in the place where we use the counter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 260.7,
          "end": 262.37,
          "en": "With that we can save that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 262.37,
          "end": 266.053,
          "en": "and now if I reload, you see this works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 267.66,
          "end": 270.12,
          "en": "And that's how easy it is to use Vuex,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 270.12,
          "end": 271.743,
          "en": "with the composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
